window.docContents[129].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.HkdfSalt/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___HkdfSalt":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications › HkdfSalt.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 2 of 31 lines trusted trust banner B2, trusted: definitions used by the statement source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nHKDF Salt TypeTrusted: definitions used by the statement. Leaf definition of CryptoGames.HKDF.Salt, an optional 32-byte HKDF salt (none = no salt) shared between CryptoGames/AEAD/HKDFDefs.lean and LibsignalSpqr.lean without pulling CryptoGames / VCVio into the symbolic statement closure.\n\n\n\nabbrev SaltL27–28 ↗#A 32-byte HKDF salt (spqr message key); none = no salt.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/HkdfSalt.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.HkdfSalt/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___HkdfSalt"},"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Object.Placed/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Object___Placed":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Object › Placed.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the symbolic proof 5 headline theorems depend on it 493 of 662 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nDeclarations on this page (54)def nopWorddef tlsdescAdrPage21Worddef tlsdescLd64Lo12Worddef tprelHi12Worddef movwSignedWorddef movwNcWorddef TlsUInt32InRangedef TprelHi12InRangedef TprelLo12InRangedef TprelG1InRangedef TprelG0InRangedef CodeRelocInRangedef patchRelocWorddef addSignedAddrdef isAdrpWorddef isAddImm64Worddef isBWorddef adrTemplatestructure CodeBlockstructure PlacedLibstructure Placementdef resolvedef relocAt?def targetdef wordAtdef relaxableAtdef gotPairAtdef tlsieRelaxableAtdef patchGotOrTlsIeRelaxeddef b2bNext?def relocTargetdef undefWeakBranchdef relaxedAtdef patchedWorddef patcheddef relocInRangestructure Placeabledef PlacedLib.patchDataRelocdef dataRelocWidthdef PlacedLib.programstructure MultiPlacedLibdef MultiPlacedLib.elfSymstructure MultiPlacementdef lookupBlockSymAuxdef lookupBlockSymdef MultiPlacedLib.resolvedef MultiPlacedLib.blockPlacementdef MultiPlacedLib.blockLibdef MultiPlacedLib.patchDataRelocdef MultiPlacedLib.patchedDatadef RangesDisjointstructure MultiPlacedLib.Placeabledef MultiPlacedLib.blockProgramdef MultiPlacedLib.fnAddr\n\nPlaced Libraries: Layout-Generic Relocatable CodeModels a library as relocatable object code and data before linking (Obj.CodeBlock, Obj.PlacedLib, Obj.MultiPlacedLib), byte-slice memory mapping (Obj.HoldsBytes), and the output of a static linker (ld.lld) placing code at base and resolving external and data symbols through ρ (Obj.Placement, Obj.PlacedLib.Placeable, Obj.CodeBlock.patched, Obj.PlacedLib.program, Obj.PlacedLib.patchedData). Covers AArch64 ADRP+ADD to NOP+ADR, GOT, and TLS linker relaxations (Placement.relax), branch-to-branch retargeting (Placement.b2b), and undefined weak references (Placement.undefWeak).ModelA PlacedLib is one rigid text block (CodeBlock: the concatenated .text* input sections of the library's objects, in link order, with alignment padding) plus data objects (SymDataInfo: one per .rodata/.data/.bss input section or merged-section piece). A Placement chooses:* base: the text block's address (no page alignment is assumed);* ρ: the address of every symbol not defined in the block (data objects, extern functions);* relax: for each relaxable ADRP+ADD pair (by ADRP byte offset), whether the linker relaxed it;* b2b: for each branch whose target is a block B, whether the linker retargeted it to that B's target;* undefWeak: for each weak reference (CodeBlock.weakRefs), whether the linker left it undefined (direct branches to it then branch to the next instruction). Every code relocation (including branches inside the block) is applied by CodeBlock.patched with targets addSignedAddr (resolve sym) addend. Placeable collects the conditions under which a linker applies the relocations without overflow; a contract over PlacedLib.program assuming Placeable holds for every such link. Whether some real binary is such a link is a separate, checkable fact (Obj.PlacedLib.InElf).AuditingSoundness of a library theorem about a real binary rests only on PlacedLib.program, PlacedLib.fnAddr, PlacedLib.dataInit and PlacedLib.InElf (bytes and permissions in the ELF). The relocation, relaxation and branch-to-branch model (patchedWord, Placeable) only affects completeness: if it disagrees with what the linker emitted, InElf fails on the real bytes (or the theorem is harder to prove), but it cannot make a false claim about those bytes.\n\n\n\nRelocation word patching\n\ndef nopWordL58–59 ↗#The NOP instruction word (0xd503201f).\n\ndef tlsdescAdrPage21WordL61–64 ↗#R_AARCH64_TLSDESC_ADR_PAGE21 relaxed to Local-Exec (TLSLE): movz x0, #((target >> 16) & 0xffff), lsl #16.\n\ndef tlsdescLd64Lo12WordL66–69 ↗#R_AARCH64_TLSDESC_LD64_LO12 relaxed to Local-Exec (TLSLE): movk x0, #(target & 0xffff).\n\ndef tprelHi12WordL71–73 ↗#Patch 32-bit ADD Xd, Xn, #imm12, lsl #12 template w for R_AARCH64_TLSLE_ADD_TPREL_HI12.\n\ndef movwSignedWordL75–85 ↗#Patch 32-bit MOVZ/MOVN template w with signed target shifted right by shift bits (R_AARCH64_TLSLE_MOVW_TPREL_G1 at shift = 16, R_AARCH64_TLSLE_MOVW_TPREL_G0 at shift = 0): sets bit 30 (MOVZ) when 0 ≤ target.toInt, or clears bit 30 (MOVN) and encodes ~~~target when target.toInt < 0.\n\ndef movwNcWordL87–91 ↗#Patch 32-bit MOVK template w with unchecked 16-bit slice target >>> shift (R_AARCH64_TLSLE_MOVW_TPREL_G1_NC at shift = 16, R_AARCH64_TLSLE_MOVW_TPREL_G0_NC at shift = 0).\n\ndef TlsUInt32InRangeL93–95 ↗#Propositional range condition ([0, 2^32)) for TLSDESC → TLSLE relaxation.\n\ndef TprelHi12InRangeL97–99 ↗#Propositional range condition ([0, 2^24)) for R_AARCH64_TLSLE_ADD_TPREL_HI12.\n\ndef TprelLo12InRangeL101–103 ↗#Propositional range condition ([0, 2^12)) for R_AARCH64_TLSLE_ADD_TPREL_LO12.\n\ndef TprelG1InRangeL105–107 ↗#Propositional signed range condition ([-2^32, 2^32)) for R_AARCH64_TLSLE_MOVW_TPREL_G1.\n\ndef TprelG0InRangeL109–111 ↗#Propositional signed range condition ([-2^16, 2^16)) for R_AARCH64_TLSLE_MOVW_TPREL_G0.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 113–117): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesArm64.Obj.tlsBaseOffset\n\ndef CodeRelocInRangeL119–147 ↗#Propositional range/alignment condition for a general code relocation kind at place targeting target.\n\ndef patchRelocWordL149–178 ↗#Patch a 32-bit instruction template w at address place for relocation kind targeting address target.\n\ndef addSignedAddrL180–182 ↗#Compute symAddr + addend in 64-bit two's-complement arithmetic (symAddr when addend = 0).\n\ndef isAdrpWordL184–185 ↗#w is an ADRP Xd, #imm (1 immlo 10000 immhi Rd).\n\ndef isAddImm64WordL187–188 ↗#w is a 64-bit ADD Xd, Xn, #imm12 with no shift (1 0 0 100010 0 imm12 Rn Rd).\n\ndef isBWordL190–191 ↗#w is an unconditional branch B #imm (000101 imm26).\n\ndef adrTemplateL193–194 ↗#The ADR Xd, #0 template with destination register rd (0 00 10000 0...0 Rd).\n\nCode blocks\n\nstructure CodeBlockL198–215 ↗#One library's text, as a rigid block of relocatable code:* code: the bytes of the library's .text* input sections, concatenated in link order with alignment padding, before relocation (relocated fields hold the assembler's values);* align: the alignment the linker gives the block (its largest input-section alignment);* symbols: the functions it defines and their byte offsets in code;* relocs: its code relocations (RelocEntry.off is a byte offset in code); a relocation whose symbol is in symbols targets base + off, any other symbol resolves through ρ;* externs: functions it calls but does not define;* weakRefs: the subset of externs that the objects reference as undefined STB_WEAK symbols (a linker may leave these undefined, see Placement.undefWeak).\n\nstructure PlacedLibL217–224 ↗#A library: its text block, its data objects, and the functions it exports (whose .symtab entries a linked binary must keep).\n\nstructure PlacementL226–249 ↗#Where a linker placed a library: text at base, every other symbol at ρ sym, which relaxable pairs/sites (by byte offset in the block) it relaxed, and which branches (by byte offset) it retargeted past a block B (branch-to-branch).The symbol map ρ sym gives:* the symbol's virtual address for direct code/data relocations, relaxed GOT (GotToNopAdr / GotToAdrpAdd) sites, data objects (PlacedLib.data), and extern stubs;* the GOT-slot virtual address for unrelaxed GOT (adrGotPage / ld64GotLo12Nc) and unrelaxed initial-exec TLS (tlsieAdrGottprelPage21 / tlsieLd64GottprelLo12Nc) sites; and* the thread-pointer (TPIDR_EL0) offset for relaxed initial-exec TLS (TLSIE → MOVZ/MOVK), TLSDESC → TLSLE, and direct local-exec TLS (TLSLE) sites. undefWeak sym says the linker left the weak reference sym (one of the block's weakRefs) undefined: a direct call26/jump26 to it is then patched to branch to the next instruction (AAELF64 §5.7.11.2, as ld.lld -static does), while its GOT sites still load the GOT slot at ρ sym (which then holds 0). (Mixed relaxed+unrelaxed GOT accesses to the same symbol, GOT-loading a PlacedLib.data symbol, or a direct branch to a defined weak symbol that is also GOT-loaded unrelaxed, would require a separate GOT-slot map if ever needed.)\n\n\n\ndef resolveL253–257 ↗#Address of sym under placement pl: base + off for a block symbol, else pl.ρ sym.\n\ndef relocAt?L259–261 ↗#The relocation at byte offset off, if any (the first one; Placeable requires uniqueness).\n\ndef targetL263–265 ↗#Relocation target sym + addend under pl.\n\ndef wordAtL267–268 ↗#The unrelocated 32-bit word at byte offset off.\n\ndef relaxableAtL270–283 ↗#The words at off and off + 4 form an ADRP Xd, sym + ADD Xd, Xd, :lo12:sym pair that a linker may relax to NOP + ADR Xd, sym (R_AARCH64_ADR_PREL_PG_HI21 and R_AARCH64_ADD_ABS_LO12_NC with the same symbol and addend, 64-bit unshifted ADD, and the same general-purpose register Xd != 31 as ADRP destination, ADD source and ADD destination, since register 31 encodes SP in ADD but XZR in ADR).\n\ndef gotPairAtL285–302 ↗#The words at off and off + 4 form a GOT-load ADRP Xd, :got:sym + LDR Xd, [Xd, :got_lo12:sym] pair (R_AARCH64_ADR_GOT_PAGE and R_AARCH64_LD64_GOT_LO12_NC with the same symbol, addend 0, 64-bit unsigned LDR, and the same general-purpose register Xd != 31 as ADRP destination, LDR base and LDR destination, matching lld/ELF/Arch/AArch64.cpp tryRelaxAdrpLdr). A linker may relax the pair to NOP + ADR Xd, sym (pl.relax off = true, pl.relax (off + 4) = false), to ADRP Xd, sym + ADD Xd, Xd, :lo12:sym (pl.relax off = false, pl.relax (off + 4) = true), or leave it as an unrelaxed GOT load (pl.relax off = false, pl.relax (off + 4) = false).\n\ndef tlsieRelaxableAtL304–320 ↗#The word at off has an initial-exec TLS relocation (R_AARCH64_TLSIE_ADR_GOTTPREL_PAGE21 on ADRP Xd or R_AARCH64_TLSIE_LD64_GOTTPREL_LO12_NC on LDR Xd, [Xd, ...]) that a static executable linker may relax to local-exec MOVZ Xd, #:tprel_g1:sym, LSL #16 or MOVK Xd, #:tprel_g0_nc:sym when pl.relax off = true. Requires Rn == Rt on the LDR (matching standard compiler codegen; lld/ELF/Arch/AArch64.cpp relaxTlsIeToLe relaxes regardless of Rn, so Rn != Rt safely stays unrelaxed; Rd = 31 is XZR in ADRP, LDR, MOVZ, and MOVK).\n\ndef patchGotOrTlsIeRelaxedL322–330 ↗#Relocated word for a relaxed GOT or initial-exec TLS relocation site.\n\ndef b2bNext?L332–346 ↗#Branch-to-branch candidate: branch relocation r (call26/jump26) targets a block word that is an unconditional B with a jump26 relocation r2; a linker may then retarget the branch to r2's target (BL f where f: B g becomes BL g, same behaviour).\n\ndef relocTargetL348–353 ↗#Target of relocation r at byte offset off under pl: r2's target if pl.b2b off and r is a branch-to-branch candidate (b2bNext? r = some r2), else blk.target pl r.\n\ndef undefWeakBranchL355–359 ↗#Relocation r is a direct branch (call26/jump26) to a weak reference of the block (weakRefs) that pl leaves undefined (pl.undefWeak); the linker then patches it to branch to the next instruction instead of to relocTarget (AAELF64 §5.7.11.2).\n\ndef relaxedAtL361–363 ↗#The pair at off is relaxed under pl.\n\ndef patchedWordL365–391 ↗#The relocated word at byte offset off under placement pl:* the ADRP of a relaxed ADRP+ADD pair becomes NOP, its ADD becomes ADR Xd, sym + addend;* a GOT pair (gotPairAt) or initial-exec TLS relocation (tlsieRelaxableAt) is relaxed according to pl.relax (GotToNopAdr, GotToAdrpAdd, or TlsIeToLe);* any other relocated word is patched by patchRelocWord at place = base + off, targeting place + 4 for a direct branch to an undefined weak reference (undefWeakBranch) and relocTarget (which applies branch-to-branch) otherwise;* unrelocated words are unchanged.\n\ndef patchedL393–396 ↗#The relocated bytes of the block under placement pl.\n\ndef relocInRangeL398–427 ↗#Range and alignment condition for relocation kind at byte offset off (place = base + off) targeting target in blk under placement pl:* for .adrGotPage: True when relaxed to NOP + ADR (gotPairAt off && pl.relax off), or AdrpInRange place target otherwise;* for .ld64GotLo12Nc: AdrInRange place target when relaxed to NOP + ADR (4 ≤ off && gotPairAt (off - 4) && pl.relax (off - 4)), True when relaxed to ADRP + ADD (4 ≤ off && gotPairAt (off - 4) && pl.relax off), or Lo12Aligned 3 target when unrelaxed;* for .tlsieAdrGottprelPage21 / .tlsieLd64GottprelLo12Nc: TlsIeInRange target when relaxed to local-exec (tlsieRelaxableAt off && pl.relax off), or CodeRelocInRange kind (AdrpInRange / Lo12Aligned 3) when unrelaxed;* for all other relocation kinds: CodeRelocInRange kind place target.\n\nstructure PlaceableL429–451 ↗#A linker placing the block under pl applies every relocation without overflow:* base is aligned to align (a positive multiple of 4), the block does not wrap, and its length is a multiple of 4;* relocations are at distinct, 4-aligned, in-bounds offsets and are code relocations (not abs64/abs32) whose targets (relocTarget) satisfy relocInRange (also for an undefWeakBranch site, which is conservative: the linker does not range-check it);* each relaxed pair's ADR (at base + off + 4) reaches its target (AdrInRange);* block symbols are 4-aligned and in bounds, distinct from externs, and every extern resolves outside the block.\n\n\n\nData objects\n\ndef PlacedLib.patchDataRelocL457–467 ↗#Apply data relocation r (abs64, abs32, prel32; others leave bytes unchanged) to the bytes bytes of a data object placed at addr.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 469–473): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesArm64.Obj.PlacedLib.patchedData\n\ndef dataRelocWidthL475–479 ↗#Width in bytes of a data relocation (0 for non-data kinds).\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 481–495): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesArm64.Obj.PlacedLib.Placeable.text, Arm64.Obj.PlacedLib.Placeable.data_relocs_ok, Arm64.Obj.PlacedLib.Placeable, Arm64.Obj.PlacedLib.Placeable.data_nodup, Arm64.Obj.PlacedLib.Placeable.data_ok\n\nThe placed program\n\ndef PlacedLib.programL499–512 ↗#The library placed under pl as a Program: the patched text at pl.base, its symbols, a hook entry point for each extern e at pl.ρ e (consulted via externs), and override hooks overrides for its own functions.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 514–516): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesArm64.Obj.PlacedLib.fnAddr\n\nMulti-block placed libraries\n\nstructure MultiPlacedLibL520–530 ↗#A library as several independently placed code blocks, its data objects, and the symbols it exports to callers. exportSyms maps an export (named as in blocks' symbols, e.g. a demangled Rust path) to its raw .symtab name in the objects (e.g. the mangled symbol) when the two differ (elfSym).\n\ndef MultiPlacedLib.elfSymL532–534 ↗#The raw .symtab name of export e of lib: its exportSyms entry, or e itself.\n\nstructure MultiPlacementL536–550 ↗#Linker-chosen parameters for placing a MultiPlacedLib:* base i: runtime start address of block i (blocks[i]);* ρ sym: runtime address of any symbol sym outside blocks (data objects and externs);* relax i off: whether the ADRP+ADD pair at byte off of block i was relaxed to NOP+ADR;* b2b i off: whether the unconditional branch (b26/call26) at byte off of block i, targeting an unconditional B (b26) in block i, was retargeted to that B's target;* undefWeak sym: whether the weak reference sym was left undefined (Placement.undefWeak).\n\ndef lookupBlockSymAuxL552–558 ↗#First (blockIdx, off) pair for symbol name across blocks, searching from startIdx.\n\ndef lookupBlockSymL560–562 ↗#First (blockIdx, off) pair for symbol name across blocks.\n\ndef MultiPlacedLib.resolveL564–570 ↗#Runtime address of symbol sym under multi-block placement mpl: mpl.base i + off if sym is at offset off in block i, otherwise mpl.ρ sym.\n\ndef MultiPlacedLib.blockPlacementL572–580 ↗#Projected single-block Placement for block i of lib under mpl: placed at mpl.base i, with all other blocks' symbols and external/data symbols resolved through lib.resolve mpl.\n\ndef MultiPlacedLib.blockLibL582–587 ↗#Block i of lib viewed as a single-block PlacedLib sharing lib.data and lib.exports.\n\ndef MultiPlacedLib.patchDataRelocL589–599 ↗#Apply data relocation r (abs64, abs32, prel32; others leave bytes unchanged) to the bytes bytes of a data object placed at addr under mpl.\n\ndef MultiPlacedLib.patchedDataL601–605 ↗#The initial bytes of data object d under mpl: its relocated bytes followed by d.zeroTail zero bytes, at address mpl.ρ d.sym.\n\ndef RangesDisjointL607–609 ↗#Two half-open address ranges [b1, b1 + n1) and [b2, b2 + n2) in Nat do not overlap.\n\nstructure MultiPlacedLib.PlaceableL611–632 ↗#A linker placing the multi-block library under mpl applies every relocation without overflow:* every block i is Placeable under its projected lib.blockPlacement mpl i;* distinct blocks occupy disjoint address ranges;* symbol names across all blocks are distinct (symbols_nodup);* data object symbols are distinct, not block symbols, aligned at mpl.ρ d.sym without wrapping, and each data relocation is an in-bounds, in-range abs64/abs32/prel32.\n\ndef MultiPlacedLib.blockProgramL634–639 ↗#Block i of lib placed under mpl as a Program.\n\ndef MultiPlacedLib.fnAddrL641–647 ↗#Runtime address of block symbol name under mpl (mpl.base 0 if name is not a block symbol).\n\n2 declarations not shown (lines 649–660): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesArm64.Obj.HoldsBytes, Arm64.Obj.MultiPlacedLib.CodeLoaded\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Object/Placed.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Object.Placed/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Object___Placed"}});